<title>HONG KONG: KEXIM to price US$500 mln global bond on Tuesday.</title>
<headline>KEXIM to price US$500 mln global bond on Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-02-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>A US$500 million five-year global bond for the Export-Import Bank of Korea (KEXIM) will be priced during New York hours today, joint lead manager and bookrunner Morgan Stanley said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The bond matures on February 10, 2002. It will be priced to yield 44-46 basis points over the five-year U.S. Treasury note.</p>
<p>Salomon Brothers is the other joint lead and bookrunner.</p>
<p>Daiwa, Lehman Brothers, Merrill Lynch and SBC Warburg are co-lead managers. Chase, CS First Boston, DKB, DG Bank, Fuji, Kasi, LTCB, Sanwa and Tokyo-Mitsubishi are co-managers.</p>
<p>The payment date is February 10.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong Newsroom (852) 2843 6371</p>
</text>
